```
This sets the margin to fill the container, but `m_width` stays 40. So this adjusts MARGIN not width. So m_width=40, but m_marginRight becomes 60. Then `offsetWidth`=40 (correct), and offsetLeft... the margin pushes nothing.

But wait — my `naturalW = child->width() + marginLeft + marginRight` = 40 + 0 + 60 = 100! That's the bug. The auto-margin-fill sets m_marginRight=60, so my naturalW includes it = 100.

For grid items, this block-level margin auto-fill shouldn't apply (`cb->isFlexibleBox()` is checked but not grid). The fix: exclude grid containers from this margin-fill, OR compute naturalW using only the content width (not margins) for grid.

The cleaner fix: add `&& !cb->isRenderGrid()` to that condition so grid children don't get margin-filled. Let me do that:

